      "kind": "review",
      "heading": "‘Primetime’",
      "films": [
        {
          "title": "Primetime",
          "year": 2026,
          "note": "Lance Oppenheim's scripted debut, built from Ajone Singh's script off Luke Dittrich's 2007 Esquire piece. Pattinson plays Chris Hansen with Dracula and Jerry Maguire in the read; Skyler Cazando's Decoy Dan is the film's conscience and near co-lead. A descent-into-madness media movie shot on roughly 20 to 25 formats, funny and sad at once and pointed about entrapment, conspiracy, and what it costs to be good at this job. It ends with the district attorney (Alex Winter) taking his life while Merritt Weaver's producer is already asking whether she can 'make it work.'"
        }
      ]
